## Context
Eight questions found as an untracked note, `questions for future work.txt`, on the doudou
clone of the old-name repo zoteus-fts5 during the 2026-11-09 erg claims rollout clone sweep
(harness tracker 1478). Filed verbatim as a ticket on the author's decision to process the
leftovers; the note's date is unknown (the clone was 2469 commits behind).

## Questions
1. Is this needed at all? Zotero has an active PR on semantic search.
2. Chunking. Zotero does structured text extraction lazily, on PDF read.
   2.1 How? Is the extractor good enough?
   2.2 Can we use this to chunk structurally? How?
   2.3 Do their chunker and ours add a context preamble to chunks?
3. Do we track the embedder and the exact document version in chunks?
4. What is the CLI like?
   4.1 Bash discoverable through --help for an LLM, or a server?

## Exit criteria
- [ ] each question answered in a design note or turned into its own ticket, or closed as moot
